WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.896
The saved school reading index assigns eleven Week 10 rows. Each guide below keeps its book, chapters, pages and focus visible, then explains the main learning ideas in English and Chinese.
学校保存的阅读索引指定了第10周十一项阅读。下面每个指南都保留书名、章节、页码和重点，并以中英文解释核心内容。

00:00:13.896 --> 00:00:27.504
This is a bilingual learning aid, not a replacement for the assigned text. If the exact school edition is unavailable or a candidate page points to a different topic, the mismatch is stated instead of silently corrected.
本指南是双语学习辅助，不能替代指定教材。若无法确认学校版本，或候选页码指向不同主题，会明确说明差异，而不是悄悄改写。

00:00:27.504 --> 00:00:59.376
The recovered course copies now identify the actual VSM and CPSC page contents. VSM includes the visible older-adult documentation task, while the CPSC literal pages cover oxygen and an attribution page rather than the named intimate routes. The complete named rectal and vaginal section is taught separately. The March2025 and June2026 BCPEG copies agree on these four assigned cards; current service details remain a separate layer.
找回的课程副本现已确定VSM及CPSC实际页内容。VSM含可见老年记录任务，CPSC指定页则是氧合及署名页，而非点名私密途径；完整点名直肠和阴道节另行讲解。2025年3月及2026年6月BCPEG在此次四张指定卡上相同，现行机构细节仍是单独一层。

00:00:59.376 --> 00:01:34.344
All eleven assigned readers now contain source-specific English and Chinese explanations. The service export includes behavioral transfers and palliative symptom care beyond the five named codes. The remaining differences are explicit: the cardiovascular locator is unavailable in the identified book, some chapter labels do not match literal page topics, and nursing procedures do not create paramedic authority. Use the explained literal ranges and separately identified named topics without pretending their locators are identical.
十一项指定读本现均提供针对来源的中英文讲解。机构导出本除点名的五项代码，还包括行为问题转院及姑息症状照护。剩余差异已明确：已识别心血管教材不含所列页码；部分章节标签与指定页主题不同；护理操作也不赋予急救员权限。应使用已讲解的实际指定范围及另行识别的点名主题，不能假装页码定位相同。

00:01:34.344 --> 00:01:46.296
BCPEG is the saved school-exam snapshot for LOC, critical history, Entonox and methoxyflurane. Its medication language is a reading target, not a stand-alone order.
BCPEG是学校保存的意识水平、关键病史、Entonox及甲氧氟烷考试快照。药物内容属于阅读目标，不是独立医嘱。

00:01:46.296 --> 00:02:00.552
Current BCEHS guidance and current legislation govern practice. Verify the school’s adopted revision with the instructor. A historical page, nursing procedure or topic label does not create PCP authority.
临床实践以BCEHS现行指南及现行法律为准。学校采用版本应向教师核实。历史页码、护理操作或主题名称不会创造PCP权限。

00:02:00.552 --> 00:02:12.816
First open the assigned source and read the surrounding context, not only the sentence that matches a keyword. Identify what the source actually claims and which provider or setting it describes.
先打开指定来源并阅读上下文，不要只找匹配关键词的句子。辨别原文真正主张什么，以及它描述的是哪类执业者或场景。

00:02:12.816 --> 00:02:24.792
Then close the text and explain the concept in your own English words. Restate it in Chinese while preserving the key English clinical term. Finish with a new application question.
随后合上文本，用自己的英文解释概念，再用中文复述并保留关键英文临床术语，最后完成一道新的应用题。

00:02:24.792 --> 00:02:38.688
The Week 10 theme connects agitation, refusal and palliative care. A behavior change can be medical; a refusal can be capable; and a palliative goal does not remove the need to assess an acute change.
第10周主题把躁动、拒绝与姑息照护连接起来。行为改变可能源自医学问题；拒绝可能来自具备能力的患者；姑息目标也不免除对急性变化的评估。

00:02:38.688 --> 00:02:50.496
Across all sources, keep three boundaries visible: the patient’s own goals, the current legal/service pathway, and the limits of the available edition or assigned pages.
所有来源都要保留三条边界：患者本人的目标、现行法律/服务流程，以及教材版本或指定页码的局限。

00:02:50.496 --> 00:03:23.040
The school names arrhythmia risk in psychiatric crisis. The actual cardiovascular chapter provides rhythm and electrolyte mechanisms, not a dedicated psychiatry page at the assigned locator. Connect those mechanisms to the real patient: distress and exertion can increase demand, while illness, medicines, substances or fluid losses may add risk. A psychiatric history does not explain away collapse, abnormal breathing, poor perfusion or a changing ECG.
学校点名精神危机中的心律失常风险。实际心血管章节提供心律及电解质机制，不是在指定定位处的精神科专页。应连到真实患者：痛苦及用力可增加需求，疾病、药物、物质或液体丢失又可增加风险。精神病史不能解释掉倒地、呼吸异常、灌注差或ECG变化。

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:48.864
Obtain the actual exposure timeline and a technically credible recording when indicated, while continuing immediate support. Do not diagnose a drug-induced rhythm from a medicine list or assume a normal first measurement ends the concern. Describe the observed change, relevant symptoms and uncertainty, reduce avoidable exertion and request the appropriate help through the current behavioural and medical pathways.
有指征时应取得实际暴露时间线及可靠记录，同时继续即时支持。不能从药单诊断药物诱发心律，也不能认为首次数值正常就不需关注。应描述观察变化、相关症状及不确定性，减少可避免的用力，并通过当前行为及医学路径寻求适当协助。

00:03:48.864 --> 00:04:22.752
QT spans ventricular activation and recovery, and QTc applies a specified rate correction. A prolonged interval can raise concern, but does not mean that torsades must occur. Torsades is not every polymorphic ventricular tachycardia, and the school source’s old mandatory six-hundred-millisecond wording is not a universal definition. Interpret the preceding rhythm, measurement quality, symptoms and broader context rather than measuring through a chaotic tachycardia as if it were a normal beat.
QT涵盖心室激动及恢复，QTc应用明确的心率校正。间期延长可引起担忧，不代表必然尖端扭转。尖端扭转不等于所有多形室速，学校来源旧的必须六百毫秒说法也不是通用定义。应解释前述节律、测量质量、症状及更广背景，不能把混乱快心律当正常心搏测量。

00:04:22.752 --> 00:04:54.096
Low potassium or other electrolyte changes, relevant medicines and concurrent illness can alter risk, but a waveform cannot give a serum concentration or identify one cause. In an original fainting-and-distress case, assess breathing and circulation, confirm the recording and seek appropriate assistance. Do not invent an electrolyte dose. Do not abruptly stop chronic therapy. Do not select a sedating medicine merely because a class name appears in the history.
低钾或其他电解质改变、相关药物及并存疾病可改变风险，但波形不能给出血浓度或确定唯一病因。原创近晕厥伴痛苦案例中，应评估呼吸循环、确认记录并寻适当协助。不能编造电解质剂量，不能突然停长期治疗，也不能仅因病史有某药类就选择镇静药。
